---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Local SEO for Medical Practices | Medical Rank" description="Local SEO services for US medical practices. Improve your Google Business Profile, local listings and practice website with a clear scope of work.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="pagehead">
      <h1>Local SEO for medical practices.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Help nearby patients find accurate information about your practice, the care you offer and how to contact you.</p>
      <p>Medical Rank works with US practice owners and decision makers on their Google Business Profile, local listings and practice website. We start with your services, locations and current search presence, then agree on the work to prioritize.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk about your practice</a>
        <a class="btn quiet" href="#scope">Explore the work</a>
      </div>
    </header>
  </div>

  <section class="section" id="scope">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Build a clearer local presence.</h2>
      <p class="intro">The scope follows your practice's needs. These are the parts we look at together before deciding what to change.</p>
      <div class="cols">
        <dl class="deflist">
          <div><dt>Google Business Profile</dt><dd>Review your practice details, categories, services and contact information, then improve the profile where information is incomplete or out of date.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Local listing accuracy</dt><dd>Check the practice information patients find across relevant listings, including the name, address, phone number and website.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <dl class="deflist">
          <div><dt>Practice website pages</dt><dd>Review the pages for your services and locations, with attention to useful information, clear contact details and the next step a patient can take.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Visibility and enquiry reporting</dt><dd>Agree on which reports will help assess progress. We explain what the available measures count and where a connection to appointments remains unknown.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <h2 class="label">Where we begin</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><div><strong>Understand your practice</strong>Discuss the services and locations you want patients to find, your priorities and any existing agency work.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Review the starting point</strong>Look at your Google listing, practice website and the reports you already have.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Agree on priorities</strong>Define the changes, responsibilities and measures before the engagement begins.</div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="label">Useful for the first conversation</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>Your practice website and Google Business Profile.</li>
          <li>The services and locations you want to focus on.</li>
          <li>Any current SEO reports or agency scope.</li>
          <li>What you would like to improve and what is unclear today.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note">You can enquire before you have all of this. Start with the practice and the question you are trying to answer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Before we work together.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Is this for one practice location or a small group?</summary>
          <p>We work with independent physicians, specialty clinics and small multi-location practices in the United States. Tell us about your locations and how their marketing is managed so we can discuss an appropriate scope.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need Google Ads as well?</summary>
          <p>That depends on your practice and priorities. We can discuss <a href="/services/google-ads/">Google Ads</a> alongside local SEO, then agree on what to address first.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is the work priced?</summary>
          <p>We discuss the practice's locations, current setup and work needed, then outline a scope and fee before you decide whether to proceed.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you guarantee a particular ranking?</summary>
          <p>No. Search results depend on factors no agency controls. We agree on the work, explain how it will be assessed and review what the available evidence shows.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <p class="note">For questions you can use to evaluate your current setup, see our <a href="/medical-seo/">local search resources</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Let's talk about your local search presence.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Tell us where your practice is based, what you want to improve and what you are doing today. Our first conversation is about where to start and whether we can help. No obligation.</p>
      <a class="btn quiet" href="/contact/">Talk about your practice</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
